CARCASS.

AMERICAN COMMANDED CYPRIOT UNITS HAVE ASSUMED CONTROL OF 
TERRITORY NORTH OF MT. OLYMPUS. FRENCH AND BRITISH FORCES 
HAVE ALREADY BEEN LOST IN 12 HOURS OF HEAVY FIGHTING.

1ST TROOP IS ORDERED TO INITIATE A HARD STRIKE INTO THE NATO 
FORCES OCCUPYING THE SECTOR. YOUR INITIAL COURSE WILL BE ON A
SOUTH AND EAST HEADING OF APPROXIMATELY 164ø. PRIMARY TARGET IS 
TO BE THE FIELD COMMAND TACTICAL OPS ENCAMPMENT OF ENEMY UNITS 
OPERATING IN THIS REGION. 

2ND TROOP IS ORDERED TO ASSUME A COURSE HEADING OF 109ø EAST AND 
SOUTH. YOUR PRIMARY TARGETS ARE NATO ARTILLERY PLATFORMS HOLDING
THE REGION NORTH OF THE ENEMY TACOPS ENCAMPMENT. 

2ND TROOP IS FURTHER AUTHORIZED TO ASSUME A COURSE HEADING SOUTH AND 
WEST OF ENEMY ARTILLERY PLATFORM. THIS WILL BRING 2ND TROOP IN 
CONTACT WITH ENEMY TACOP FIELD ENCAMPMENT. 2ND TROOP IS AUTHORIZED 
TO AID 1ST TROOP IN THE NEUTRALIZING OF ALL ELEMENTS WITHIN THIS AREA 
OF OPERATIONS.
